SUMMARY:CFL/Cambridge Socio-Legal Group Seminar: 'The evolution of parentho
 od in Brazil: from the single-parent stigma to multiple parenthood'
LOCATION:Faculty of Law\, David Williams Building
URL:https://www.law.cam.ac.uk/events/cflcambridge-socio-legal-group-seminar
 -evolution-parenthood-brazil-single-parent-stigma
CATEGORIES:Law
DESCRIPTION:Faculty of Law\nTopics: Law\nDetails: https://www.law.cam.ac.uk
 /events/cflcambridge-socio-legal-group-seminar-evolution-parenthood-brazil
 -single-parent-stigma\nSign-up only to join online: https://us02web.zoom.u
 s/webinar/register/WN_DSc1d-YWQsWZRVUM8s5EKg\nDate/time: \n\n Monday 25 Ja
 nuary 2027 \n\n 1:00pm to 2:00pm\n\n Location: \n\n Faculty of Law\, David
  Williams Building\n\n G24\n\n About \n\n Speaker: Professor João Costa-N
 eto (University of Brasília)\n Abstract: Brazilian family law has undergo
 ne a remarkable transformation: from a system built around marriage\, biol
 ogical descent and exclusive parenthood to one increasingly willing to rec
 ognise families as they are actually lived. This talk will trace that evol
 ution\, focusing on the rise of socioaffective parenthood and the idea tha
 t being a parent may result not only from biology\, but also from care\, r
 esponsibility and the social reality of family life. It then explores the 
 most striking consequence of that shift: multiple parenthood\, under which
  biological and socioaffective parents may coexist with equal legal status
 . Drawing on constitutional change\, legal scholarship and recent case law
 \, we wil
END:VEVENT
